{"edges":[],"nodes":[{"area":null,"id":"scope:NumberTheory/linear-recurrences/lucas-sequences-primitive-divisors/composite-terms-of-shifted-lucas-sequences","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Composite terms of shifted Lucas sequences"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:NumberTheory/linear-recurrences/lucas-sequences-primitive-divisors/divisibility-properties-of-lucas-sequences","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Divisibility properties of Lucas sequences"},{"area":null,"id":"NumberTheory/linear-recurrences/lucas-sequences-primitive-divisors/fib-prime-dvd-fib-of-legendre-sub","kind":"node","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.fib_prime_dvd_fib_of_legendre_sub","status":"fully_proved","summary":"Let $p$ be a prime with $p > 2$ and $p \\ne 5$, and let $\\left(\\frac{5}{p}\\right)$ be the Legendre symbol of $5$ modulo $p$. Then $p$ divides the Fibonacci number $F_{p-1}$ if $\\left(\\frac{5}{p}\\right) = 1$, and $p$ divides the Fibonacci number $F_{p+1}$ otherwise. Since $\\left(\\frac{5}{p}\\right) = \\pm 1$, this says that $p$ divides $F_{p - \\left(\\frac{5}{p}\\right)}$.","title":"Fibonacci prime divisibility"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:NumberTheory/linear-recurrences/lucas-sequences-primitive-divisors/large-zsigmondy-primes","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Large Zsigmondy primes"},{"area":null,"id":"NumberTheory/linear-recurrences/lucas-sequences-primitive-divisors/lengyel-fibonacci-five-adic","kind":"node","lean":"MetaMathlibExt.lengyel_fibonacci_five_adic","status":"fully_proved","summary":"Writing $F_n$ for the $n$-th Fibonacci number and $v_5$ for the $5$-adic valuation, $v_5(F_n) = v_5(n)$ for every integer $n \\ge 1$.","title":"The $5$-adic valuation of Fibonacci numbers"},{"area":null,"id":"scope:NumberTheory/linear-recurrences/lucas-sequences-primitive-divisors/lucas-sequences","kind":"scope","lean":null,"status":"can_prove","summary":null,"title":"Lucas sequences"},{"